.TH DETAB 1.SH NAMEdetab \- replace tabs with spaces.SH SYNOPSIS\fBdetab\fR[\-t\fIn\fR] [infile].SH DESCRIPTION\fBdetab\fRcopies a file, or the standard input, to the standard output with eachtab replaced by spaces up to the next tab stop.  The stops are everythree columns unless\fB\-t\fRsays otherwise..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-t\fIn\fRstops every\fIn\fRcolumns:\fB\-t8\fRfor the usual eight..SH EXAMPLES.nfdetab -t8 prog.c > prog.txtdetab -t4 < table.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOexpand, unexpand